# HTML ATTRIBUTES

1. Heading tag <h1>heading</h1>
h1 (most important heading)
h2
h3
h4 
h5
h6 (least important heading)


2. Paragraph tag <p>paragraph</p>


3. Anchor tag - used to add links to page
<a href="https://google.com">Google</a>

=> absolute link - jab dusri website ka link hota h 
=> relative link - same folder m file ho use dusri file s link kare

If the Hello.html file is located in another folder (for example, HelloFolder), we need to include the folder name in the link path, such as ./HelloFolder/Hello.html, to specify where the file is located.


4. Image tag - used to add images to your page
<img src="/image.png" alt="Random Image">

=> src - source - tells image link( can give absolute or relative link)
=> alt = alternative name for image if image is not loaded because of any reason


5. <br/> tag - Itis used to give one line space or to get content in next line


6. Bold, Italic & Underline Tags - used to highlight text in your page
<b>Bold</b>
<i>Italic</i>
<u>Underline</u>